en.statement:
Three rods of lengths a, b and c can form a triangle only when **the sum of any two of them is greater than the third**.

Read the three lengths, then print:

- `bukan segitiga` (not a triangle) when they cannot form a triangle;
- `sama sisi` (equilateral) when all three sides are equal;
- `sama kaki` (isosceles) when exactly two sides are equal;
- `sembarang` (scalene) when all three sides differ.

Examples: `3 4 5` is sembarang, `5 5 8` is sama kaki, `1 2 3` is bukan segitiga.

