en.statement:
A rectangle with sides parallel to the coordinate axes is given by **two opposite corners**. The corners can come in any order: the first one is not necessarily the lower left.

Read the two corners, then a point P. Print:

- `di dalam` (inside) when P is inside the rectangle;
- `di tepi` (on the edge) when P lies exactly on one of its sides (corners included);
- `di luar` (outside) when P is outside.

Example: corners (5, 1) and (1, 4). The point (3, 2) is inside, (1, 3) is on the edge, (6, 2) is outside.

